# Appendix A of the Reference Manual: starting Strata, environment, files.
# The appendix is kept in several parts that this one includes.  The command
# lines of the Editor, the Printer and the Viewer are not a supported way to
# start Strata: they are in the last part, between the lines that begin with
# the directives for the build type, which the release edition leaves out.
.doc Strata Reference: Starting Strata, Environment and Files
.chapter A
.h1 Starting Strata, Environment and Files [appcmd]
This appendix says how Strata is started, the environment variables that
Strata looks at, the other programs that are used, and the files that are read
and written.
.ix Starting Strata
.ix Environment variables, overview
.ix Appendix A
.h2 The parts of Strata [appcmd-glance]
.ix Program list
.ix Installed programs
Strata is started with the Document Manager.  The other parts are opened when
they are needed.
.table 18 12 29
Part | Kind | Purpose
The Editor | Interactive | Edits a document.
The Document Manager | Interactive | The master menu ({n:str}).  It
 | | starts the Editor.
The Printer | Batch | Document to PDF through LaTeX.
The Viewer | X11 only | Shows the pages of a Preview.
.end

.h3 The terminal version and the X11 version [appcmd-versions]
.ix Terminal versus X11
.ix Differences between the versions
.ix Terminal build
.ix X11 build
The Editor and the Document Manager come in two versions.  The terminal
version runs in the terminal of the shell ({n:appterm}); the X11 version
opens a window ({n:appx11}).  The two versions read the same files.  The
Printer is the same for both.  The Viewer exists only for X11: without it, or
without a display, Preview shows that the Viewer is missing.  The differences
that a user meets are in {x:appterm-diff}.  The X11 version alone reads the
environment variables {c:STRATA_X11_*}.  Keep the programs together in one
directory.


.h2 Starting Strata: the Document Manager [appcmd-str]
.ix Document Manager, command line
.ix Document Manager, options
Strata is started with the Document Manager, which is described in
{x:str}; this section gives its options and its exit status.
.h3 Options of the Document Manager [appcmd-str-opt]
.table 13 47
Option | Meaning
{c:-h}, {c:--usage} | Write a usage text on the standard output and end with status 0.
{c:--version} | Write the name and the version of the program and, on a second
 | line, the version of the file format that it writes ({c:file format 3}),
 | and end with status 0.
{c:-H PATH} | The help file, instead of the one that the search finds
 {c:--help-file PATH} | ({n:str-help-search}).
{c:--default-colors} | Use the colors that the program is delivered with and not
 | those of the settings; the variable {c:STRATA_DEFAULT_COLORS} does the same.
DOCUMENT | Put DOCUMENT in the field Document Name of the panel
 | Edit / Preview / Print Document.  Nothing is opened.
.end
.h3 Exit status of the Document Manager [appcmd-str-exit]
.ix Exit status, Document Manager
.table 8 52
Status | Meaning
0 | Quit from the menu, or {c:-h}.
1 | No interactive terminal or X display.
.end
The same table is in {x:str-exit}.
